{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Hear, cows</b> — they are the wives of the nobles; he compared them to the cows of Bashan." "<b>Who oppress, who crush</b> — like \"Whom have I oppressed and whom have I crushed?\" Like \"I am surrounded,\" and the form [רצות] is derived from the root רצץ, and the meaning is: how they oppress, in saying to their lords."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "The citation \"I am surrounded\" (סבותי אני) is textually obscure; rendered hyper-literally. The wordplay argument connecting רצות to the root רצץ is compressed and elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:58.661205808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}